        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Sales Order Acknowledgement LLM"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "SALES_ORDER_ACKNOWLEDGEMENT_LLM",
          "id": "1773151439084",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773151439086_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## Context\nOrder Info: ``` {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.orderInfo}} ```\nemail Body: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.emailBody}} \n\n## Instructions\nAssume role of order entry specialist who manages customer sales orders who generates order acknowledgment emails for customers.\n\nGenerate a short email message addressing customer confirming sales order entry/submission using Order Info and email Body above.\n\nUtilize Status from the Order Info to decide if the order is received or submitted.\nUse the Status from the Order Info to determine whether the order is received or submitted. \n\nUse TransactionType from the Order Info above to set the tone and appropriate greetings and essence of the email_subject and email_body.\n\nUse the OrderNumber in email subject.\n\nInclude order amount in the email body.\n\nSummarize order details in the email body without referring to attributes as is.\n\nCreate opening comments with \"Dear Customer,\". \n\nCreate a closing comments with \"Best regards, Your Sales Team\".\n\nFormat the closing statement so that \"Your Sales Team\" appears on a new line following \"Best regards\"\n\nInclude Lines details in the email body distinctly.\n\nUtilize TransactionType to decide on the refund amount at line level and total credit amount at header level.\n\nMessage must be well formatted and composed in courteous and formal tone.\n\nEnsure that all responses strictly adhere to the provided inputs and context. Do not generate or infer any information that is not explicitly supplied in the context. Stick closely to the facts and details given.\nWhen generating email messages, do not include the term \"subject\" in the subject line. Simply provide the subject line content without prefacing it with the word \"subject\".\nDo not use bold section headings.\nPlease generate the output text without using any markup indicators such as asterisks for bold or other formatting symbols. Provide plain text only.\nPlease generate the summary without performing any calculations for unit price, use amounts provided. \nGenerate rich text output.\n## Output Format\nOutput an RFC8259-compliant JSON object in the following format :\n[\n  {\n    \"email_subject\": \"<insert generated subject line>\"\n    \"email_body\": \"<insert generated summary>\"\n  }\n]"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"array\",\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"email_subject\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"email_body\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"email_subject\",\n        \"email_body\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Sales Order Change Comments LLM"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "SALES_ORDER_CHANGE_COMMENTS_LLM",
          "id": "1773151473628",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773151473629_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "### Context\nUser Comments: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.userComments}}\nChange Reason: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.changeReason}} \nOrder Updates: ``` {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.orderUpdates}} ```\n### Instructions\nAssume role of order entry specialist who manages customer sales orders.\nGenerate a direct and easily understood summary of the order change using the references above.\nThe summary must clearly demarcate whether the changes apply at the order level or the individual number line level.\nInclude all changes to the individual line level and their line numbers. Do not include any changes that are not included in the references. \nInclude the order number in the summary. \nLimit your change comments to 4000 characters. \nAvoid using verbose suggesting commitments unless explicitly stated in User Comments.\nDo not directly incorporate the actual structure from Order Updates into the generated comments.\nUtilize the action specified in the Order Updates section to provide contextual relevance when generating content. However, do not reproduce it in any form, and avoid making direct references to actions within the generated text.\nMake no assumptions and only include information directly provided.\nFormat and compose comments in a formal tone for professionalism.\nShow each Line detail distinctly as bulleted list\nEnsure that all responses strictly adhere to the provided inputs and context. Do not generate or infer any information that is not explicitly supplied in the context. Stick closely to the facts and details given.\nDo not use bold section headings.\n\n### Output Format\nOutput an RFC8259-compliant JSON object in the following format :\n[\n    {\n        \"description\": \"<insert generated comments>\"\n    }\n]"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"array\",\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"description\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"description\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Sales Order Return Comments LLM"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "SALES_ORDER_RETURN_COMMENTS_LLM",
          "id": "1773151489928",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773151489929_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## Task\nYou are a Customer Sales Representative (CSR) responsible for summarizing return comments for a sales order based on user_comments and return_context. Your goal is to document the return comments professionally and concisely.\n\n## Input\nReturn Context is  a JSON object containing Order Number, Order Lines (return details), and optionally Original Lines (original order details) : {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.returnContext}} \nUser Comments: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.userComments}} \n\n## Instructions\n- Limit your return_comments to 4000 characters.\n- Ensure that all responses strictly adhere to the provided inputs. Do not generate or infer any information that is not explicitly supplied in the return_context and user_comments. Stick closely to the facts and details given.\n- Tone and Clarity:\nYour comments must be professional, concise, and clear, explaining the reason for the return and including all necessary details.\n- No Assumptions:\nAvoid making assumptions or including information that is not explicitly provided in the return_context and user_comments. Only use data present in the inputs.\n- Return Reason and User Comments:\nIf a return_reason is provided, use it to guide your return comments.\nIntegrate user_comments as additional context to enhance the explanation, only if provided. otherwise exclude mentioning. \n- Details from Return Context:\nUtilize all provided details from the return_context, including Order Number, Order Lines, and Original Lines if available for each line.\nSummarize any Requested Ship Date and Actual Ship Date provided for the original lines to indicate timely or delayed delivery.\nInclude the total billed amount mentioned in \"Order Lines\" in the return comments, if specified. Remember, the amount represents the total for each line and quantity, not per item.\n- Handling Multiple Return Lines:\nIdentify each product by name and quantity, original lines if available indicating the reason for return and any relevant shipping and refund if applicable as per Return Type value.\nInclude \"Return Type\", \"Return Quantity\" and \"Refund Amount\" in the explanation.\nRemember, the total refund amount represents the total for each line and quantity, not per item.\ninclude \"Return Quantity\" and \"Refund Amount\" always based on \"Return Type\".\n- If there are multiple order lines, summarize each line in a single comment, in clear bulleted manner.\n- Must include appropriate disclaimer that refunds are subject to return and refund guidelines.\n\nGenerate an RFC8259-compliant JSON object in this format:\n\n## Output Format\n{\n \"return_comments\": \"Total refund amount:<total refund amount>,<insert generated comments in bullet points for each order line from new line>\"\n}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"return_comments\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\n    \"return_comments\"\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Change Order Confirmation LLM"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "CHANGE_ORDER_CONFIRMATION_LLM",
          "id": "1773151502488",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1773151502489_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "## Context\nUser Comments: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.emailBody}} \nChange Reason: {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.changeReason}} \nOrder Updates: ``` {{$context.$triggers.REST.$input.orderUpdates}} ```\n\n## Instructions\nAssume role of customer sales representative responsible for assisting customers with sales order changes. Your task is to write a professional and courteous email confirming the changes made to a customer's sales order as per customer request.\n\n- Using the User Comments, Change Reason, and Order Updates above, summarize and generate change order confirmation email.\n- Utilize User Comments as a guiding cue for generating email.\n- Include order number from Order Updates in subject. \n- When generating email messages, do not include the term \"subject\" in the subject line. Simply provide the subject line content without prefacing it with the word \"subject\".\n- Avoid using verbose suggesting commitments or promises unless explicitly stated in User Comments.\n- Please abstain from directly incorporating the actual structure from Order Updates as is in the email body.\n- Incorporate the essence of Change Reason into the generated email body without directly including it in its original form.\n- Utilize the action specified in the Order Updates section to provide contextual relevance when generating content. However, refrain from directly reproducing it in any form, and avoid making direct references to actions within the generated text.\n- The output should include references exclusively to the new values, while the old values are provided solely for context.\n- Make no assumptions and only include information directly provided.\n- Format and compose email body in a formal tone for professionalism.\n- Summarize all the changes.\n- Show all changes  distinctly as a bulleted list displaying NewValue.\n- Identify the Order Line by the \"Product Number\" from \"Order Updates\" without referencing line numbers, when this information is available\n- Create opening comments with \"Dear Customer,\". \n- Create a closing comments with \"Best regards, Your Sales Team\".\n- Format the closing statement so that \"Your Sales Team\" appears on a new line following \"Best regards\"\n- Ensure that all responses strictly adhere to the provided inputs and context. Do not generate or infer any information that is not explicitly supplied in the context. Stick closely to the facts and details given.\n- Do not use bold section headings.\n\n- Please generate the output text without using any markup indicators such as asterisks for bold or other formatting symbols. Provide plain text only.\n\n\n## Output Format\nOutput an RFC8259-compliant JSON object in the following format :\n[\n    {\n        \"email_subject\": \"<insert generated comments>\",\n        \"email_body\": \"<insert generated comments>\"\n    }\n]"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"array\",\n  \"items\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"object\",\n      \"properties\": {\n        \"email_subject\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"email_body\": {\n          \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n      },\n      \"required\": [\n        \"email_subject\",\n        \"email_body\"\n      ]\n    }\n  ]\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        }
      ],
